   "l": "So: one who goes about his business in the Way —\nthe man of the Way is one with the Way;",
   "v": true,
   "i": "So with the man who goes about his business in the Way: the man of the Way is at one with the Way;",
   "n": "從事於 X is a set construction, 'to engage oneself in X', and 從事 is bound here because 'follow' plus 'affairs' does not add up to it on its own. Then 者 twice over: it turns everything in front of it into a noun, so 道者 is 'the one who is of the Way', a class of man. Many editions print this line without the second 道者 — simply 故從事於道者，同於道 — and the Wang Bi text we follow repeats it. The doubling is clumsy, and may be a copyist's eye slipping; nothing hangs on it."
  },
